1
00:04:42,857 --> 00:04:48,857
Be careful who you pray to.

2
00:09:25,714 --> 00:09:31,714
The Unholy is a horror, mystery film directed by Evan Spiliotopoulos.

3
00:14:08,571 --> 00:14:14,571
Alice is a young hearing-impaired girl who, after a supposed visitation from the
Virgin Mary, is inexplicably able to hear, speak and heal the sick.

4
00:18:51,428 --> 00:18:57,428
As word spreads and people from near and far flock to witness her miracles, a disgraced
journalist hoping to revive his career visits the small New England town to investigate.

5
00:23:34,285 --> 00:23:40,285
When terrifying events begin to happen all around, he starts to question if these
phenomena are the works of the Virgin Mary or something much more sinister.

6
00:28:17,142 --> 00:28:23,142
Gerry Fenn, played by Jeffrey Dean Morgan.

7
00:32:59,999 --> 00:33:05,999
Alice, played by Cricket Brown.

8
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
Father Hagan, played by William Sadler.

9
00:42:25,714 --> 00:42:31,714
Natalie Gates, played by Katie Aselton.

10
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
Bishop Gyles, played by Cary Elwes.

11
00:51:51,428 --> 00:51:57,428
Delgarde, played by Diogo Morgado.

12
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
The Unholy is a 2021 American supernatural horror film written, produced, and directed by Evan
Spiliotopoulos (in his directorial debut), based on the 1983 novel Shrine by James Herbert.

13
01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:23,142
Produced by Sam Raimi through his Ghost House Pictures banner, it stars Jeffrey Dean Morgan,
Katie Aselton, William Sadler, Diogo Morgado, Cricket Brown, and Cary Elwes.

14
01:05:59,999 --> 01:06:05,999
The film follows on a disgraced journalist (Morgan) who discovers a series of seemingly divine miracles in a small New
England town and uses them to resurrect his career, though those "miracles" may have a much darker source.

15
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
The project was announced in December 2018 under the working title Shrine,
with Sony Pictures adapting Herbert's novel of the same name.

16
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
The cast was announced between 2018 and 2020, with principal photography commencing in Boston,
but on March 14, 2020, filming was suspended because of the COVID-19 pandemic.

17
01:20:08,571 --> 01:20:14,571
The Unholy was theatrically released in the United States on April 2, 2021.

18
01:24:51,428 --> 01:24:57,428
Despite receiving negative reviews from critics, the film was considered a box office
success, grossing $31 million worldwide against a budget of $10 million.

19
01:29:34,285 --> 01:29:40,285
The film explores themes of witch, melancholy, demon, mysterious, shocking.

20
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
The tone is dark and mind_bending.
